d{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{18-16}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85171/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd" :answer/id #uuid "baa34db1-5970-5aa4-b084-0352a869408e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6305ec90-193f-577d-875a-7066776262e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cfab445-ffaf-5c68-8be7-c89c236ff4ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317429/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd" :answer-field/choices ["q-317429/field-1/fc5c11d990f3318da393f8e6ca9ca48c0d82b2f6c13de974653c16fa7068aacd" "q-317429/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429/field-2/b2610da8893659d718854e37078f3eb0696d92ccd388407c31b8014819c1d06a" :answer/id #uuid "2aed8cee-ed81-5be7-9b26-c8fe2d2b0134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "79655dbc-b505-53f2-ad4b-8f78e546db9d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317429/field-2/b2610da8893659d718854e37078f3eb0696d92ccd388407c31b8014819c1d06a" :answer-field/choices ["q-317429/field-2/b2610da8893659d718854e37078f3eb0696d92ccd388407c31b8014819c1d06a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317429" :question/id #uuid "4bf62a04-752f-5b6c-afdb-534f8df78167" :question/math-academy-id "q-317429" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{12+10}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{11} \\\\ \\frac{19}{22}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317429/field-1" "q-317429/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "00c44b4c-e34f-50bc-9625-41c29776eb9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9716162c-5b0f-57e1-88ea-bf0cb95f2b77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "33d9b464-0f9e-50ae-a095-50d2b6538733" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "a0de5b9f-d890-5e1b-b316-fdf28ff903ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2c1c5245-8b77-5f5d-9eea-2cdb2accd99a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1316c83c-b72a-50b4-bdbc-2de0845dfa18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12273/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-12273/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-12273/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-12273/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-12273/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-12273/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12273" :question/id #uuid "98953b86-1970-5f9b-baa4-31123d8311f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-12273" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n\n- $(-5,-2)$\n- $(-6,-3)$\n- $(-8,-4)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 & -8 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(-5,-2),(-6,-3),(-8,-4),(-7,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-12273/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12273"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a4690e49-98cb-500a-8a24-2a5450a75394" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "776c663b-0fbb-54b2-9cf3-976f43c93aef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "1498a4c9-87e4-5710-a9a2-9ef8d1924f63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f763be17-07f9-5202-929d-0569f45dad17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c0b43e18-f376-51a5-b559-7275d6dd9404" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5584d02d-df96-50c4-89a3-b26deebd1b8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9262/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-9262/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-9262/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-9262/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-9262/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-9262/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9262" :question/id #uuid "965eaccb-b8c7-5f4b-a1ea-f7ee3a9791ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-9262" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(2,-5),(3,-6),(4,-8),$ and $(3,-7).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\n- $(1,3)$\n- $(3,3)$\n- $(2,3)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0-1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & -8 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,2),(3,3),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9262/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d8d70f60-3b31-5a23-a530-e4b4fbf03eff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ac9ab4f6-655f-5818-9d98-0406f23b03ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b05b4f64-0a6b-5987-aff1-8038340059ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "2eec686d-7f4a-52ad-bf7f-ecce79e7a494" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "158f054f-766a-5ffe-b731-3f1d88b0d02d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5ea3ee6-c419-50f1-b790-79f416f0de76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9258/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-9258/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9258/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-9258/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-9258/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9258/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9258" :question/id #uuid "6142d263-231c-53b8-832c-47907c585c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-9258" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(4,-1),(17,-3),$ and $(10,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(-1,1)$\n- $(5,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-0}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9258/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9258"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
